384 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The filament of a 3D printer is the material used for printing objects. It typically comes in spools and is available in various types, each offering unique properties suited for different applications. The most common filaments are PLA \(Polylactic Acid\), known for being easy to print and environmentally friendly, and ABS \(Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene\), which is durable and heat-resistant. Other filaments include PETG \(Polyethylene Terephthalate Glycol\), TPU \(Thermoplastic Polyurethane\)for flexible prints, and *nylon* for strong, high-performance applications. Filaments are typically available in different diameters \(e.g., 1.75mm or 3mm\) and come in various colors and finishes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
