396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Nozzle of a 3D printer is a crucial component that controls the extrusion of melted filament onto the print bed. It is typically made of metal, such as brass, and has a small opening \(often ranging from 0.2mm to 1mm in diameter\) through which the filament flows. The nozzle heats up to the required temperature, melting the filament, which is then deposited layer by layer to form the object. The size of the nozzle affects print speed and detail: smaller nozzles produce finer details, while larger ones print faster with thicker layers. Proper maintenance of the nozzle is essential for consistent print quality.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0]
>>
