<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The  cooling fan of a 3D printer plays an important role in controlling the cooling and solidification of the printed material. It is usually located near the hot end or nozzle and blows air onto the printed layers as they are extruded. This helps the material cool and harden quickly, especially for filaments like PLA that need rapid cooling to maintain their shape and reduce warping. In some 3D printers, cooling fans are adjustable or have multiple fans to improve print quality, especially for fine details or overhangs. Proper cooling is essential for achieving smooth, high-quality prints.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
