420 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The 3D printer bed \(also known as the print bed or build platform\) is the surface on which the object is printed. It provides a stable foundation for the material to adhere to as the print progresses layer by layer. The bed can be made from materials like glass, aluminum, or heated surfaces, with heated beds being common to improve adhesion and reduce warping. A heated bed helps prevent the first few layers from cooling too quickly, which can lead to print failures. Some beds are coated with materials like PEI or Kapton to further enhance adhesion, while others use magnetic or removable flexible surfaces for easy print removal. Proper leveling of the bed is crucial for successful prints.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
