432 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The filament feeder \(also known as the extruder feeder\) is a key component of a 3D printer that controls the feeding of filament into the hot end for extrusion. It consists of a motorized mechanism that pulls the filament from the spool and pushes it through the extruder and hot end. This ensures a continuous flow of material to be melted and deposited onto the print bed. Filament feeders typically use gears or wheels to grip the filament and push it consistently. Some printers use direct drive extruders, where the feeder is directly attached to the hot end, while others use Bowden extruders, where the filament is fed through a tube to the hot end. Proper calibration of the filament feeder ensures consistent extrusion and high-quality prints.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
