482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The future of 3D printing holds immense potential across industries. In manufacturing, it could enable on-demand, localized production, reducing waste and costs. In healthcare, advancements may lead to custom prosthetics, medical devices, and even bioprinted tissues and organs. Construction could see affordable, 3D-printed homes, addressing housing shortages. The food industry may utilize 3D printing for personalized nutrition and sustainable food products. In fashion and art, it will foster innovative designs. As education adopts 3D printing, it will enhance creativity and hands-on learning. Overall, the technology will transform production methods, drive sustainability, and enable limitless customization.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [1]
>>
